**Read:** [Principles of Extractive Metallurgy — Tarun Kumar Kundu, NPTEL](../sources/Principles-of-Extractive-Metallurgy-NPTEL.lingua#r_7VCNEHN5VCQDDQTZ512PSHFZ78), the complete solvent-extraction and refining sequence; [Non-ferrous Extractive Metallurgy — Ray and Pugazhenthy, NPTEL](../sources/Nonferrous-Extractive-Metallurgy-NPTEL.lingua#r_29G1ZF58Y8EG123MNX3ZRNRE2W), the full solution-purification and relevant metal cases; [Extractive Metallurgy of Copper — Schlesinger, Sole, Davenport, and Alvear Flores](../sources/Extractive-Metallurgy-of-Copper.lingua#r_47NCQVYD4J2DXH9AV48XDMNHJ7), all of chapter 15 and the connected leach/electrowinning chapters, when available; [Non-ferrous Metals Industries — European Commission BREF](../sources/Nonferrous-Metals-Industries-BREF.lingua#r_19ZD7KKDWVWM20MXVNCQZJMCDB), a whole applicable extraction/stripping circuit case.

Solvent extraction partitions a solute between immiscible liquid phases through a defined chemical mechanism. Distribution ratio, selectivity, loading, extractant state, acidity, ligands, temperature, and phase ratio need explicit definitions. A ratio reported at one composition is not necessarily constant over a whole loading/stripping circuit.

Reuse the refining phase-inventory balance, now distinguishing aqueous and organic volumes/concentrations and their chemical species. For ideal fixed D = c_org/c_aq, initially solute-free organic volume O contacting aqueous volume A, the aqueous fraction remaining is A/(A+DO) under equilibrium and unchanged phase volumes. Actual nonlinear isotherms and finite loading require their own balances.

Extraction, scrubbing, and stripping serve different quality and transfer duties. Mixing, residence, phase disengagement, entrainment, emulsion/crud formation, carryover, degradation, and reagent/water recycle affect observed performance. An equilibrium-stage construction is distinguished from demonstrated stage efficiency and stable operation.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete primary extraction/stripping study or industrial circuit. Derive stage and recycle accounts, reproduce the distribution/loading evidence with uncertainty, and compare an alternative staging/phase-ratio arrangement. Independently check conservation and limiting behavior, then test performance on withheld composition conditions. Explain how co-extracted impurities and physical phase separation affect the final electrowinning/refining task.

